// VSCO 2 CE expanded section: horn, oboe, contrabass, harp, struck timpani,
// timpani roll and suspended cymbal.
// Upstream: sgossner/VSCO-2-CE, revision 440300901dfe9275fd84e0b7763af1f8443ae62e (CC0-1.0).
// Recordings are fetched by install.py into the gitignored assets/ directory.

// Original CC0 VSCO recordings; source files remain unchanged.
// Calibrated pitch and leading-silence offsets. Sustains use 0.4–2.8 s mono RMS;
// harp and struck timpani levels use the strongest 50 ms RMS in their first 0.5 s.
// Harp names use scientific octaves; horn/oboe/bass names are one octave lower.
// Horn has sparse native coverage between C4 and D5. Bass below E1 is transposed.
// Timpani root is its principal resonant mode; low G1–D2 uses downward transposition.
// Cymbal: C4 triggers full 9.628 s crescendo; maximum 100 ms RMS at 3.8 s.

